WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.163
SIEM stands for Security Information and Event Management.

00:00:03.163 --> 00:00:08.141
The information component focuses on collecting, storing, and managing logs and security data.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:12.353
The event management component focuses on identifying meaningful activity through searches,

00:00:12.353 --> 00:00:13.885
correlations, alerts, and investigations.

00:00:13.885 --> 00:00:19.629
SIEM platforms combine these functions to help security teams transform raw data into operational awareness.

00:00:19.629 --> 00:00:22.309
Instead of looking at individual systems separately,

00:00:22.309 --> 00:00:26.521
analysts can investigate activity across the environment from a centralized interface.

00:00:26.521 --> 00:00:31.499
A SIEM is best understood as an operational capability, not a magic product.

00:00:31.499 --> 00:00:36.477
It is useful when the right data is collected, normalized, searched, correlated, tuned,

00:00:36.477 --> 00:00:39.540
and reviewed by people who understand the environment.
